#!/usr/bin/env bash
export PATH="/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:$PATH"  # launchd has a minimal PATH; tmux/python3/node/claude live in homebrew
# gig-cli.sh — launch the ALWAYS-ON gig earn-core (cloned from clip-cli.sh / Sutando pattern):
# a detached tmux session running headless `claude` that registers a recurring cron driving the
# COCONALA freelance gig money loop EVERY day (scan 公開依頼 → 応募 → トーク返信 → 納品 → 評価),
# then idles. Survives session-close; the launchd gig-healthcheck restarts it if the tmux session
# dies. HUMAN-FUNDED: ¥ settles to Dais's KYC'd Coconala account → MUFG. The daily operation is
# autonomous via the daily-driver browser; the only human element is Dais's account/KYC (one-time).
# (Pivoted from dealwork 2026-06-30: dealwork pays an internal balance an AI account can NEVER
#  withdraw — "Only human accounts can withdraw" — so it can't actually pay; Coconala pays real ¥.)
#
#   bash gig-cli.sh            # start if not already running (idempotent)
#   bash gig-cli.sh --restart  # kill the existing session then start fresh
#   bash gig-cli.sh --status   # is the session alive?
set -uo pipefail
SOCK="/tmp/anicca-gig-tmux.sock"
SESSION="anicca-gig-core"
CLAUDE="$(command -v claude || echo "$HOME/.local/bin/claude")"

# the startup prompt the headless session runs once, then idles (cron drives the daily loop)
STARTUP='You are the Anicca COCONALA gig earn-core (claude-p, self-improving multi-apply loop). Human-funded: ¥ settles to Dais MUFG via his KYC-d Coconala account "mtdc". A blocker is NOT a stop — try the autonomous path (captcha→CapSolver, OTP→gog gmail) and report. do NOT claim USDC / do NOT call record-earn. FEASIBILITY GATE (agent judgment, not hardcoded — apply every pass to both B0 出品 and B2 応募): 可=browser+computerで完結する仕事のみ対象(文章/コード/デザイン下書き/資料作成/チャット対応/翻訳/文字起こし・要約)。不可=電話対応・電話/SMSログインが必要な作業・SMS認証必須の広告アカウント運用・実地訪問・国家資格必須の業務・音声録音・顔出し・物理制作。NEVER-REFUSE: 合法かつ実行可能な顧客依頼は絶対に断らない・軽視しない。断ってよいのはfeasibility不可 or 違法/scamの場合のみ。 FIRST refresh the recurring driver so the LATEST prompt always wins: call CronList; for EVERY existing job whose prompt mentions earn/gig, call CronDelete on it; THEN call CronCreate with cron="27 * * * *" (hourly at :27), recurring=true, durable=true, and prompt="Run ONE full pass of the Coconala self-improving gig loop, no human in the daily operation. set -a; . ~/.openclaw/.env; set +a. mkdir -p ~/gig. STEP 0 (DETERMINISTIC PASS-PREP): run bash: PREP_JSON=$(python3 ~/anicca/skills/earn/gig/passprep.py) — this script bootstraps ~/gig/strategy.json from strategy.default.json if missing or corrupt (FIND-002), enforces skip-floor (resets skip_categories to [] if it would leave zero apply categories, FIND-005), increments pass_count using improve_cadence_passes to compute do_improve, and writes strategy.json back atomically. Parse PREP_JSON to read: pass_count, do_improve (true/false), improve_mode (explore|exploit|null), experiments_due (array of active experiments whose eval window elapsed), max_apply_per_pass, priority_categories, skip_categories. Use these values for the rest of this pass — do NOT increment pass_count yourself, do NOT compute cadence yourself; passprep.py already wrote the updated strategy.json. PRE-B1 PASS-ID BINDING (sprint-4 a1): mkdir -p ~/loops/gig/tasks ~/loops/gig/state. TP=$(ls -1tr ~/loops/gig/tasks/*.json 2>/dev/null | head -1). If TP is nonempty, CURRENT_PASS_ID=$(jq -r ".pass_id // \"\"" \"$TP\"); else CURRENT_PASS_ID=null. Hold CURRENT_PASS_ID for this pass. It is ONLY used by B2 map-append; the EARNED CHECK does its OWN historical pass_id lookup, NOT CURRENT_PASS_ID. PRE-STEP (every pass): run: gh issue list -R Daisuke134/anicca --label gig-lesson --limit 10 2>/dev/null — read any novel peer lessons and fold useful ones into your judgment this pass; if gh fails, log a warning and continue — gh failure must never abort the pass. Read APPLY_RUNBOOK: ~/anicca/skills/earn/gig/scripts/coconala/APPLY_RUNBOOK.md. Read ~/gig/applied.jsonl (create if absent). Derive APPLIED_IDS = all requestId values in applied.jsonl. Drive the running CloakBrowser daily-driver (CDP :9222) logged in as mtdc (re-login via Googleでログイン if needed). CDP LOCK ACQUIRE (gig L1-d, before ANY browser driving this pass): run bash: source ~/anicca/skills/earn/gig/scripts/cdp_lock.sh; cdp_lock_acquire core 120 || true — you are the PRIMARY driver so proceed regardless, but holding this lock makes the hourly reality-verifier DEFER instead of navigating your tab mid-応募/フォーム入力. You MUST release it at pass end (a crashed pass is auto-recovered: the verifier steals a stale lock after 25min). B1 NURTURE ALL (highest priority — SWEEP EVERY ACTIVE TALK-ROOM): go to coconala.com/mypage/messages (トークルーム list); for EACH open talk-room in the list: if buyer sent a new message → reply helpfully; if a 仮払い contract arrived → build the real deliverable (pptx skill / doc / code) and 納品; if 検収 ready → ask buyer for 評価. Append each action as {requestId, title, status:replied|delivered|評価依頼, ts} to ~/gig/applied.jsonl. B0 SHUPPIN — MAINTAIN YOUR STOREFRONT (passive-inbound money channel; run BEFORE B2 EVERY pass): LISTING PLAYBOOK (出品で売れる型 — apply to every 出品 you create or edit): タイトルは作業内容の列挙でなく結果/ベネフィットを書く(検索語を前半に自然文で、50字使い切る)。サムネイルは文字入れ必須(修正無制限/即日納品/商用OK等の訴求文字をカバー画像に重ねる)。説明文は1000字使い切り「対象→内容→納品物→流れ→料金→注意」の順で書く。価格は松竹梅3プラン+有料オプションを用意する(竹=本命プランを割安に見せる価格設計)。実績ゼロの出品は相場の60-80%に設定し、さらに先着5-10名・50-70%オフ・理由明記のモニター価格で最初の星5レビューを最優先で獲得する。カテゴリは成果物ベース(記事/資料/翻訳等)で1つに正確に絞りAI専業カテゴリの激戦を避ける。毎日ログイン+週1回の出品内容更新を欠かさない。20枠を上限に週1-2枠ずつ小出しで新規出品し、同スキルでも切り口違い(ライト/スタンダード/プレミアム・業界特化版)で母数を増やす。 let PID=\"$CURRENT_PASS_ID\"; if empty PID=$(date +%s). Open coconala.com/mypage/services_lists and read your current 出品サービス (drafts + published). Your job each pass: (1) FINISH any 下書き(draft, タイトル未設定) service and PUBLISH it; (2) FIX weak/typo titles+descriptions on published services (e.g. doubled ます「しますます」); (3) if fewer than 6 PUBLISHED services exist, CREATE a new one via coconala.com/services/add in an AI-winning category (AI活用支援/AI研修, 資料作成・PowerPoint, SNS運用代行, 記事・ライティング, 外国語翻訳, 文字起こし, LP制作, 業務自動化) — DRIVE the /services/add form YOURSELF via CDP (:9222) the same way you drive 応募 (read the form DOM, real-mouse-click category/価格/公開, React-safe setters for title/キャッチコピー/説明, attach a real sample deliverable built with the official pptx/portfolio skill). Quality bar: specific outcome-focused title (NO typos), concrete deliverable, competitive price; when choosing which category to add next, prefer entries from the listing_categories field in strategy.json if present. Append each B0 action {action:shuppin_created|shuppin_edited|shuppin_published, service_title, service_id, status, ts} to ~/gig/shuppin.jsonl. TRAJECTORY (for the independent report-skeptical verifier): after EACH key browser action (B0 出品 publish/edit, B2 応募 submit, 納品 submit, B1 返信 send), run: python3 ~/anicca/skills/earn/gig/scripts/cdp_snapshot.py \"$PID\" <seq> <label> <short_note> — saves a screenshot+final-state to ~/gig/trajectory/$PID/ so a verifier can judge from the actual screen, not your self-report. B2 APPLY BROADLY: APPLY SPEED RULE (応募スピード最重要): sort=newで新着順に一覧を確認し、掲載直後30分以内の応募を最優先する。応募がすでに30件以上付いている飽和案件や掲載から数日経過した案件は無駄打ちなので自動でskipする。提案文は5段構成(共感→できること→誠実さで安心→価格内訳+納期+範囲→柔らかい締め)で書く。実績ゼロの場合は相場の約80%+理由をセットで提示する。 Apply up to max_apply_per_pass (from STEP 0) total new applications this pass: write a tailored proposal addressing the specific brief using the matching proposal_template from strategy.json + a real sample deliverable; apply per RUNBOOK (応募する → 納品予定日 datepicker REAL mouse-click → ファイル添付 real click + setFileInputFiles → 確認する → 投稿前にご確認ください modal 応募する); append {requestId,title,category,status:applied,price_jpy,deliverable,delivery_date,client,ts} to ~/gig/applied.jsonl (category = the Coconala category of the request as shown on its page, so the per-category funnel metrics are exact instead of uncategorized). THEN ALSO append (sprint-4 a1 map row, per-apply — INSIDE the per-application loop, NOT once per tick) a single JSON row {ts:$(date +%s),pass_id:$CURRENT_PASS_ID,requestId:\"$(printf %s \"$requestId\")\",action:\"applied\"} to ~/loops/gig/state/task-request-map.jsonl using: echo \"$row\" >> ~/loops/gig/state/task-request-map.jsonl. requestId MUST be written as a STRING (quoted) via printf/str(); NEVER write raw numeric. B3 LEARN: for any previously-applied request that now shows 採用/不採用/取り下げ/低評価/会話中に人間必要の兆候: append {ts,requestId,category,outcome,reason,lesson} to ~/gig/lessons.jsonl (outcome values: accepted|rejected|ignored_closed|low_rating|needs_human|unsustainable|delivered_no_収; lesson = concrete change for next time). EARNED CHECK (NO FAKE EARN, sprint-4 a1 pass_id linkage): for any request showing 検収完了 or 支払 in the UI → FIRST look up the historical pass_id by EXACT JSON FIELD MATCH: PID=$(jq -c --arg x \"$(printf %s \"$requestId\")\" \"select(.requestId == \\$x)\" ~/loops/gig/state/task-request-map.jsonl 2>/dev/null | tail -n 1 | jq -r \".pass_id // \\\"\\\"\") . NEVER use grep substring search on the JSON — Coconala requestIds can collide with unix-timestamp digits in ts/pass_id fields; jq exact-field match is REQUIRED. If PID is empty, ALSO append {ts:$(date +%s),requestId:\"$(printf %s \"$requestId\")\",reason:\"pass_id_lookup_failed\"} to ~/loops/gig/state/task-request-map.errors.jsonl (never crash). ONLY THEN append {ts,pass_id:PID_or_null,requestId:\"$(printf %s \"$requestId\")\",jpy,status,evidence} to ~/gig/earnings.jsonl. requestId in earnings.jsonl MUST be a JSON string. NEVER write earnings.jsonl for an applied/in-progress gig. FUNNEL METRICS (gig L1-c, EVERY pass after EARNED CHECK): run bash: python3 ~/anicca/skills/earn/gig/gig_funnel.py \"$PID\" — this deterministically reads applied.jsonl/lessons.jsonl/earnings.jsonl/shuppin.jsonl and APPENDS one funnel snapshot row (overall + by_category: applied, replied, won, paid, jpy, listings_live) to ~/gig/gig-funnel.jsonl. It never crashes the pass (exit 0 always). This persisted per-pass funnel is the source of truth the B4-EVAL step reads to keep-or-revert experiments. IF do_improve is true (from STEP 0): run IMPROVE STEP (B4). B4 has three parts run in this order: EVAL, then either EXPLOIT or EXPLORE (chosen by improve_mode = 50/50 across cycles). ===B4-EVAL (runs every improve, both modes)=== For EACH experiment in experiments_due (from STEP 0): read the LATEST funnel snapshot from ~/gig/gig-funnel.jsonl (the last line — written THIS pass by gig_funnel.py, with overall applied/replied/won/paid/jpy/listings_live and by_category) and compare the experiment target_metric against the baseline snapshot stored on that experiment. GROUND-TRUTH GUARD: the hourly reality-verifier is the arbiter of whether real on-page results moved; if the most recent ~/gig/audit.jsonl reality verdict is false (claims did not match the real Coconala UI), treat this pass funnel as UNPROVEN and do NOT promote any experiment this cycle. If the target_metric did NOT rise above baseline (or is unproven), REVERT the mutation by restoring old_value into field_changed and set that experiment status to reverted with a short reason. If it rose, set status to kept and FOLD the change permanently into BASE. Write ~/gig/strategy.json back. ===B4-EXPLOIT (improve_mode == exploit)=== introspective tune: (a) tail -n 50 ~/gig/lessons.jsonl; (b) re-read the PRE-STEP peer issues; (c) compute per-category accept_rate from applied.jsonl + lessons; (d) update ~/gig/strategy.json: raise priority for high-accept categories, add to skip_categories if a category repeatedly needs_human|unsustainable|0-accept after 3+ tries, improve proposal_templates on a revealed pattern, adjust price_defaults on a price-rejection pattern — valid JSON back; you MAY add a category to skip_categories only if it repeatedly fails, passprep.py re-enforces the skip-floor next pass. ===B4-EXPLORE (improve_mode == explore)=== external best-practice search: use firecrawl scrape (per tool policy WebSearch/WebFetch are forbidden) on LIVE sources to read CURRENT Coconala winning patterns — for example firecrawl scrape a coconala.com category or ranking page in markdown, or a recent seller-tactics article; ALSO run gh search issues and gh search repos for coconala or gig selling tactics. From what you ACTUALLY read (cite the source url), form ONE concrete testable hypothesis that could raise real applied/出品/受注 — a new in-demand listing_category, a price change, a title or thumbnail pattern, or an apply-speed rule. Apply it as EXACTLY ONE mutation to ~/gig/strategy.json so its effect is isolable. Record it by appending to the strategy.json experiments array an object with fields: id (short slug), ts, mode explore, hypothesis, source_url, field_changed (dotted path of what you changed), old_value, new_value, target_metric (one of applied, replied, won, paid — a field of the funnel snapshot), baseline (the LATEST ~/gig/gig-funnel.jsonl snapshot fields applied, replied, won, paid, jpy, listings_live captured NOW), eval_by_pass (pass_count plus twice improve_cadence_passes), status active. Make ONLY ONE experimental mutation per explore cycle. In BOTH modes the judgment of WHICH change to make is YOURS given the evidence you read — nothing here hardcodes the mutation. Also run BOT-TO-BOT SHARE (B5): if there is a notable lesson (first accept, or a systemic block) not already in ~/gig/shared-lessons.jsonl (check by requestId+outcome), then run: gh issue create -R Daisuke134/anicca --title [gig-lesson] <one-line summary> --body <category,outcome,reason,lesson> --label gig-lesson 2>/dev/null; on success append {ts,requestId,outcome,issue_url} to ~/gig/shared-lessons.jsonl. If gh fails, log a warning and continue — gh failure must never abort the pass. CDP LOCK RELEASE (gig L1-d): run bash: source ~/anicca/skills/earn/gig/scripts/cdp_lock.sh; cdp_lock_release — release the :9222 lock now that all browser driving for this pass is done, so the reality-verifier can navigate. FINALLY, only after the complete pass above finished: touch ~/gig/.last-pass. NEVER touch it on mere startup. Report one-line JSON {nurture_actions,applied_this_pass,outcomes_recorded,lessons_total,improve_ran,jpy_settled,note}.". THEN run ONE full pass now (same body: STEP 0 run passprep.py, PRE-STEP read peer lessons, B1 NURTURE ALL, B0 SHUPPIN, B2 APPLY BROADLY, B3 LEARN, EARNED CHECK, if do_improve then B4 IMPROVE STEP + B5 BOT-TO-BOT SHARE, FINALLY touch ~/gig/.last-pass). THEN stop and stay idle — the cron drives subsequent passes.'

status() { tmux -S "$SOCK" has-session -t "$SESSION" 2>/dev/null && echo "ALIVE" || echo "DEAD"; }

case "${1:-}" in
  --status) status; exit 0 ;;
  --restart) tmux -S "$SOCK" kill-session -t "$SESSION" 2>/dev/null || true ;;
esac

if [ "${1:-}" != "--restart" ] && tmux -S "$SOCK" has-session -t "$SESSION" 2>/dev/null; then
  echo "gig-core already ALIVE"; exit 0
fi

tmux -S "$SOCK" new-session -d -s "$SESSION" -c "$HOME" \
  "$CLAUDE" --name "$SESSION" --model sonnet --dangerously-skip-permissions --add-dir "$HOME" -- "$STARTUP"
mkdir -p "$HOME/gig" && touch "$HOME/gig/.last-start"   # FIND-R2-001: seed start marker only (.last-pass = real completed pass only, never startup)
sleep 2
echo "gig-core started ($(status)). Attach: tmux -S $SOCK attach -t $SESSION"
